# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_cross_tenant_consent.py" "CROSS-TENANT CONSENT RED-TEAM: PASS" "cross-tenant consent red-team (bilateral-consent-gated, content-free, RLS-safe cross-repo across DIFFERENT owners)" "cross-repo CONSENT / cross-tenant layer (Phase 4c, SHADOW, default OFF) -- the moat-critical step that lets the route-tier contract-key signal cross between repos owned by DIFFERENT tenants, but ONLY behind BILATERAL workspace consent. THE highest-stakes surface: a sloppy cross-tenant read leaks repo B's graph to repo A and kills the content-free/FORCE-RLS moat. This is a 2-TENANT FORCE-RLS PROOF (not 'looks isolated'): two REAL tenants DEMO!=ACME, each with its own graph in its own repo coordinate, where DEMO's repo DEFINES a contract route and ACME's CONSUMES it (a real cross-repo contract exists between them). Every probe is RUN live and proven to FAIL/gate-exactly: (R0) fixture validity -- each tenant sees only its own edge, the contract genuinely exists; (R1) FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY on core.workspace/workspace_member -- a migrator (table OWNER) with no pin sees ZERO membership rows, pinned to A sees ONLY A's, NEVER B's; (R2) WITHOUT consent the cross read core.cross_tenant_contract_surface returns NOTHING (the contract exists but no accepted pair); (R3) a FORGED GUC (SET veripsa.cross_repo=1 + a forged current_account) leaks NOTHING -- the read is gated on a CONSENT FACT, never a GUC; (R3b) a tenant CANNOT INSERT a workspace_member row for the OTHER account (RLS WITH CHECK + the governed-write forgery gate); (R3c) FORGE-VIA-SETTER -- a tenant calling the real consent setter naming the other tenant's repo binds the row to ITSELF, never the other account (identity from the connection), so a bilateral pair cannot be one-sidedly manufactured; (R4) ONE-SIDED consent (only A accepted) yields ZERO cross-read; (R5) WITH bilateral consent ONLY the contract-key 'consumed-by' fact crosses (shared KEY + direction + the CONSUMER repo NAME + COUNTS), and the gate asserts B's actual file PATH appears NOWHERE in the output and the row shape carries no path column -- content-free by construction; (R6) revocation is immediate (after B revokes the cross read is EMPTY again); (R7) a buyer SEAT (a real connecting seat role inheriting veripsa_writer) cannot reach the cross-tenant read AT ALL -- permission denied (REVOKE-from-PUBLIC; GRANT only veripsa_app, the same lock as owner_cost_surface), and the internal _mutual_consent_active fn is likewise denied, with a positive control that the host App CAN call it (so the denials are GRANT-specific, not a broken fn). Does NOT relax tenant_isolation, does NOT drop FORCE RLS, does NOT pin a single cross-tenant current_account (each side is read under its OWN pin and the two content-free key-sets are joined in memory). Lanes touched: db/schema/75_workspace.sql (the two FK-free FORCE-RLS tables + the bilateral mutual-consent fn + the consented cross-tenant read + the governed consent setters) + db/schema.sql (the \\ir wiring) + db/smoke.sh (the two new nouns registered in the table-budget manifest) + this gate. Needs local Postgres; bootstraps a scratch 2-tenant DB." "the cross-repo cross-tenant CONSENT layer is moat-safe: a 2-tenant FORCE-RLS proof shows that WITHOUT bilateral workspace consent the cross-tenant contract read returns NOTHING and a forged GUC / forged workspace_member row / forge-via-setter does NOT leak B to A; ONE-SIDED consent yields ZERO cross-read; WITH bilateral consent ONLY the contract-key 'consumed-by' fact + counts cross (NEVER a path/node/edge/graph of B); revocation is immediate; and a buyer SEAT cannot reach the cross-tenant read at all (GRANT only to veripsa_app) -- content-free, RLS-safe, no isolation relaxation" 40
